    "narrative": "For June 30, 2026, the LawDog lineup is anchored by two high-upside plays against Erich Fedde, as **Taylor Ward** (71.46) and **Dylan Beavers** (68.38) benefit from a significant park factor and a favorable matchup against a starter with a poor 5.20 xERA. **Tyler Freeman** (69.11) represents our premier speed-based play; his score is buoyed by Eury P\u00e9rez\u2019s slower delivery pace, which provides a high-probability opportunity for a stolen base, a vital metric given our league\u2019s scarcity-heavy scoring. Similarly, **Bryson Stott** (68.86) is a strong start against Chandler; while he faces an elite catcher\u2019s arm, the positive platoon split and favorable wind conditions make him a primary contributor today.\n\nThe most difficult decision for the optimizer involved the catcher and bench spots. **Yainer Diaz** (38.99) fell just below our 40-point \"Below Floor\" threshold, largely due to a tough matchup against Ryan and a drop in batting order priority, forcing him to the pine. **Jung Hoo Lee** (48.58) was the closest to cracking the starting nine, but his projected lower-third batting order position ultimately lowered his ceiling relative to **Lawrence Butler** and **Daulton Varsho**, despite their own platoon-related efficiency hits. We are monitoring **Cal Raleigh**, **Luis Arraez**, **Geraldo Perdomo**, **Matt Chapman**, and **Tyler Freeman** closely, as their scores are currently based on pending lineups; should their confirmed batting orders slide significantly, we may need to rotate in depth pieces like **Gavin Sheets** or **Drew Gilbert** to maintain our competitive edge in the 5x5 categories.",
